    "turn_text": "Yeah, so I mean, you could kind of get the political spin from that, right? Like, oh, we can do better, right? But his points are valid. And again, the polls are showing that, whether you're Republican, Democrat, independent, the polls are saying people are uncomfortable about where inflation is, people are uncomfortable where the gas prices are, people are uncomfortable with what they're spending right now, and they want answers, they want solutions. And that's exactly what his point is, is what are the steps they're going to be needed to take to get us back on track? It's not one answer, right? It's not one thing that needs to be done. And, you know, some of this is related to, you know, COVID and the response there. We had said on this show that our biggest concern that happened with that is some of the stimulus that occurred during COVID was fine with. It was the 1.7 trillion that we spent after that, that that seemed to be the fuel to the fire to light all of this inflation and all of this spending. And we need to figure out how you're going to fix that issue and get things back under control. So again, a gallon of gas doesn't become $6, $7, $8 and it becomes unaffordable for people to live, go to work, do the things they need to do. And so we've got some issues and that's relating back to the client's portfolios and the adjustments that we've needed to make to weather the storm through some of these market volatility that we're seeing. And again, I'm here to tell you it's not ready to stop. It's gonna happen some more and we've got to be prepared for it.",
