    "turn_text": "You know, it was interesting because he said Trump there, but it seemed every time he was talking about his role as vice president, he always said, you know, when I was part of the national ticket, when I was part of that. And so there's definitely some hurt feelings or some animosity or something there that he's kind of trying to distance himself from Trump. And you could tell that, but like, I don't know if you noticed, but you answer, ask a question. And, you know, he's got no shortage of words, right? I mean, he'll go on forever. You almost have to like dive in and cut in and ask him something different to redirect. But, you know, his points are valid. The question is, is what's going to be done in the near future? How does that impact things? And how do we address the real problems to get us back under control in some of these areas?",
