        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "People retain ownership and control over their property until they die.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Death alone should not determine the redistribution of assets.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "The current system of inheritance assumes unjustified entitlement to posthumous control over wealth.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      },
      {
        "text": "There is a moral issue with forcing wealth distribution at death without prior agreement.",
